# Batch files are stored verbatim, with CRLF, and never normalised.
# cmd.exe expects CRLF and can mis-parse parenthesised blocks on bare LF, so
# the safest rule is no conversion at all: the committed bytes are exactly
# what a clone, an archive, or a copy receives. `whitespace=cr-at-eol` stops
# git's whitespace check from reporting every CR as trailing whitespace.
*.bat -text whitespace=cr-at-eol
*.cmd -text whitespace=cr-at-eol
